# Build context exclusions for the API image.
# Without these, a local bin/obj (Windows-x64) would be copied into a
# Linux container and can break the publish step.

# Note: unlike .gitignore, a pattern with no "/" in .dockerignore matches only
# at the context root. Both forms are listed, because the context root IS this
# project folder - copying a Windows-built obj/project.assets.json over the
# container's own restore output is exactly what breaks the publish step.
bin/
obj/
out/
publish/
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/out/
**/publish/

# IDE and editor state
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.csproj.user

# Local secrets - never bake credentials into an image layer
appsettings.Development.json
appsettings.Local.json
appsettings.*.local.json
appsettings.Production.json
secrets.json
.env
.env.*

# Tests, docs, source-control and container files themselves
**/*.md
**/*.http
.git/
.gitignore
**/Dockerfile*
**/.dockerignore

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
